vs-imageseqs third-party notices
================================

This distribution contains the vs-imageseqs VapourSynth plugin and native
code from the projects listed below. The files in LICENSES/ are part of the
distribution and preserve the applicable license texts and notices.

The exact native inputs recorded here are from the x64-windows-static-md
vcpkg installation used to build the Windows wheel. The two Linux builds pin
dav1d, libde265 and libwebp in `tools/build-manylinux.sh` and
`tools/build-musllinux.sh`; Cargo.lock selects the embedded libheif and OpenJPEG
sources. The macOS arm64 build uses
the same pinned dav1d and libde265 source versions, builds them as shared
libraries, bundles them, and disables unused libheif codec backends so
machine-local codecs are not linked:

  * libheif 1.23.1
  * libde265 1.1.1
  * dav1d 1.5.3
  * libwebp 1.6.0
  * wpd 0.2.0, at the exact git revision named in `Cargo.toml`
  * OpenJPEG (vendored by openjpeg-sys 1.0.12)

The native dependency versions and license expressions used by this build
are recorded below. `wpd` is a Rust crate rather than a system library, but
it is listed here because its x86-64 decode routines are hand-written NASM
sources that the crate assembles and links into the plugin, so it ships the
same way the C libraries above do. The remaining Rust crate licenses are
intentionally out of scope for this notice bundle.

