final native link output after changing either dependency configuration.

Ported source code
------------------

Some of the still readers this plugin decodes with its own code are ports of
the corresponding reader in the `image` crate, version 0.25.10, which is
licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0. `image` puts no per-file header on its sources, so
the license travels with the files named here rather than inside them. The
texts are kept verbatim as LICENSES/image-LICENSE-MIT.txt and
LICENSES/image-LICENSE-APACHE.txt.

The ported files, and the upstream module each was ported from under
image-0.25.10's src/codecs/:

  src/formats/bmp.rs
      bmp/decoder.rs, bmp/mod.rs -- the palette, run-length and bitfield
      paths, and the DIB header parsing that ico.rs also uses
  src/formats/ico.rs
      ico/decoder.rs -- the directory, the entry scoring and the AND mask
  src/formats/tga.rs
      tga/ -- the header and all eleven image types
  src/formats/dds.rs
      dds/ -- the DXT1, DXT3 and DXT5 block decoding and the DX10 mapping
  src/formats/pnm.rs
      pnm/decoder.rs and pnm/header.rs -- the parser and the header, and not
      pnm/autobreak.rs, which writes a pnm rather than reading one

Each of those modules says at its head what it was ported from. The other
still readers under src/formats/ are not ports: hdr.rs is written for this
plugin, and the rest call a crate or a library directly.

Static-linking release checklist
---------------------------------

The license files and notices above satisfy the accompanying-text part of
the distribution. They do not by themselves satisfy every source and
relinking requirement that can apply to a statically linked LGPL library.
Before publishing a wheel containing this DLL, the release should also:

  1. Make the Corresponding Source for the exact libheif and libde265
     binaries available, including the build configuration and any changes.
  2. Provide the Corresponding Application Code and a practical way for a
     recipient to relink the application/plugin with a modified LGPL library,
     as required by the chosen LGPLv3 distribution route.
  3. Preserve the copyright notices, license texts, warranty disclaimers,
     and source information for all components.
The current source distribution contains this plugin's source and build
metadata, but the ignored vcpkg_installed directory is not itself a
Corresponding Source archive. Arrange an exact-source archive or a valid
written offer/source URL for every published binary as part of release work.

Each Linux build's artifacts are accompanied by a relinking source archive:
`linux-relink-source.tar.gz` for the manylinux wheel and
`linux-musl-relink-source.tar.gz` for the musllinux one. Each contains the
application and dependency sources used by that build, including the vendored
libheif and OpenJPEG sources, and the build/relink instructions in BUILDING.md.
The Linux and macOS wheels and plugin ZIPs include dav1d and libde265 as
separate shared libraries with relative loader paths. Their license texts
remain under LICENSES/. The existing Windows source/relinking requirements
above remain applicable to the static Windows binaries.

